> Sparse labels must have exactly zero loss gradient

A3D segmentation model assigns a class to every voxel,but only some slices
may be annotated. Sparse softmax CE masks unannotated voxels before weight
normalization. With class weight \(w_y\),annotation indicator \(a_i\),and
\(Z=\max(\sum_i a_iw_{y_i},10^{-6})\),

$$L_{CE}=-\frac1Z\sum_i a_iw_{y_i}\log p_{iy_i},\qquad
\frac{\partial L_{CE}}{\partial z_{ic}}=\frac{a_iw_{y_i}}Z(p_{ic}-\mathbf1[c=y_i]).$$
\alttext(Weighted cross entropy divides by the sum of annotated voxel weights;every unannotated voxel has zero logit derivative.)

For three zero-logit voxels with labels0,2,255 and weights1,2,4,the loss is
log(3),normalization is5,and the last voxel has exactly zero derivative.
Label255 means unannotated;other labels outside the class range are ignored too.
An entirely unannotated volume gives a differentiable zero loss. The native
checks independently verify every derivative,including all-void cases.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/volumetric_segmentation_sparse.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto logits = n::zeros({1, 1, 1, 3, 3}).requires_grad_();
  const auto labels = n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{0, 2, 255}, {1, 1, 1, 3});
  const auto loss = n::models::SparseVolumeCE(logits, labels, 3, n::tensor({1., 2., 4.}));
  const auto gradient = n::grad(loss, {logits})[0].reshape({3, 3});
  if (std::abs(loss.item() - std::log(3.)) > 1e-7 ||
      n::sum(n::abs(n::slice_axis(gradient, 0, 2, 3))).item() != 0)
    return 1;
  auto p = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(gradient, {0}), -.6, .6);
  p.title("Sparse voxel logit derivatives");
  p.x_label("class0,1,2");
  p.y_label("voxel0,1,2 from bottom");
  p.size(800, 600);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  p.save_svg("build/volumetric_segmentation_sparse.svg");
  std::print("Loss {:.9f}=log(3);annotated weight sum5;third voxel label255 has exactly zero "
             "gradient. No fitting.\n",
             loss.item());
}
```
