> Squared-denominator Dice is a different objective

V-Net trains foreground overlap directly. For valid voxels of volume n,write
\(A_n=2\sum_i p_it_i+\epsilon\),\(B_n=\sum_i(p_i^2+t_i^2)+\epsilon\),
with \(\epsilon=10^{-6}\). Average only volumes with at least one valid label:

$$L_D=\frac1{N_{valid}}\sum_n\left(1-\frac{A_n}{B_n}\right),\qquad
\frac{\partial L_D}{\partial p_j}=-\frac{2t_jB_n-2p_jA_n}{N_{valid}B_n^2}.$$
\alttext(Squared Dice loss averages one minus twice foreground overlap divided by the sum of squared probabilities and targets,with a small stabilizer.)

Unannotated voxel derivatives remain zero. Perfect foreground probabilities
have zero loss,and entirely void volumes are excluded. This loss is not linear
Dice or the thresholded held-out Dice metric. The example below uses two tiny
volumes and one void voxel;the native independent quotient-rule oracle checks
every probability derivative.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/volumetric_segmentation_dice.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto probability = n::tensor({.2, .5, .9, .7, .1, .4}, {2, 1, 1, 3}).requires_grad_();
  const auto labels =
      n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{0, 1, 1, 1, 255, 0}, {2, 1, 1, 3});
  const auto loss = n::models::SquaredVolumeDice(probability, labels);
  const auto gradient = n::grad(loss, {probability})[0].to_vector<double>();
  if (gradient[4] != 0)
    return 1;
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  const double low = std::min(0., *std::min_element(gradient.begin(), gradient.end())) - .1,
               high = std::max(0., *std::max_element(gradient.begin(), gradient.end())) + .15;
  p.bars({0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, gradient, "derivative", {37, 99, 235}, .6)
      .title("Squared-Dice probability gradients")
      .x_label("voxel index;index4 is unannotated")
      .y_label("d loss / d foreground probability")
      .y_limits(low, high)
      .size(850, 550);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  p.save_svg("build/volumetric_segmentation_dice.svg");
  std::print("Two-volume mean squared-Dice loss {:.9f};void voxel4 derivative exactly zero. "
             "Native independent quotient-rule/perfect/all-void checks pass.\n",
             loss.item());
}
```
