> Full-width models and anisotropic geometry

3D U-Net has four encoder stages,three cropped skips,and learned2x2x2
channel-preserving up-convolutions. Each encoder stage doubles channels before
pooling. VALID convolution pairs shrink spatial sides;132x132x116 maps to
44x44x28. The full convolution census is19,069,955 learned scalars. Replacing
convolution biases by affine BN increases the total by2,336 to19,072,291;
BN also owns separate moving moments. The initialized full-width parameter
and gradient checks below execute on8-cube SAME volumes;the original large
VALID geometry is checked arithmetically,not silently executed at that size.

V-Net retains four learned down/up stages,5x5x5 residual stacks,concatenated
skips and learned per-channel PReLU(initial slope.25,identity derivative at0).
Its full65,175,314-scalar graph executes at16-cube input. Compact base2 models
retain every stage:3D U-Net has74,828 learned scalars,V-Net1,019,348. Native
checks independently cover every3D convolution/transpose input/filter/bias
derivative,centred crop Jacobians,PReLU/shortcut behavior,volumetric BN and
all compact stage gradients.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  if (m::Unet3DOutputSide(132) != 44 || m::Unet3DOutputSide(116) != 28)
    return 1;
  for (int variant = 0; variant < 3; ++variant) {
    n::ParameterStore p(17), state(18);
    n::Tensor logits;
    if (variant < 2) {
      m::Unet3DConfig c;
      c.valid = false;
      c.batch_norm = variant == 1;
      logits = m::Unet3D(p, state, n::zeros({1, 8, 8, 8, 3}), c, true).logits;
    } else
      logits = m::VNet(p, n::zeros({1, 16, 16, 16, 1})).logits;
    const auto gradient = n::grad(n::sum(n::square(logits)), p.parameters());
    const std::int64_t expected = variant == 0 ? 19069955 : variant == 1 ? 19072291 : 65175314;
    const std::size_t tensors = variant == 0 ? 33 : variant == 1 ? 47 : 89;
    if (p.count() != expected || gradient.size() != tensors)
      return 1;
    for (const auto &g : gradient)
      if (!g.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(g.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()))
        return 1;
    std::print("Full variant{}:{} learned/{} BN state scalars,all{} finite defined "
               "gradients;executed at{}-cube SAME geometry.\n",
               variant, p.count(), state.count(), gradient.size(), variant < 2 ? 8 : 16);
  }
  std::print("Original3D U-Net VALID132x132x116 ->44x44x28 checked independently. Compact "
             "base2 models retain every encoder/decoder stage.\n");
}
```
