> Actual generated volumes and sparse fitting annotations

Twenty-four fitting/eight validation/eight test volumes use independent tensor
seeds11/22/33,each16x16x16. Centres,radii and oblique tilt are sampled before
voxel arithmetic. Foreground/background means are.8/-.8,Gaussian noise SD.12,
with a weak x ramp. Tensor RNG intentionally changes the original mt19937
fixed-seed pixels. These synthetic ellipsoids have no anatomical meaning.

The gallery shows the actual first two fitting volumes as axial,coronal and
sagittal centre slices,each paired with dense truth. U-Net optimization sees
only axial slices z=2,6,10,14:exactly25% of labels. Images remain dense.
Fitting-only inverse-square-root class weights use one pseudocount per class
and exclude all unannotated voxels;validation/test labels never enter them.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/volumetric_segmentation_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto fit = m::MakeTensorEllipsoidVolumes(24, 16, 11);
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows(24);
  std::iota(rows.begin(), rows.end(), 0);
  const auto sparse = m::TensorVolumeBatch(fit, rows, true);
  const auto weights = m::SparseVolumeClassWeights(sparse.second);
  const auto annotated = n::count_nonzero(n::less(sparse.second, 2.)).item<std::int64_t>();
  if (annotated != 24 * 4096 / 4)
    return 1;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(m::VolumeSlicePreview(fit), "build/volumetric_segmentation_data.png", 1,
                     0, 1, 3, 1., 5);
  std::print("24 fitting16-cube volumes;{} of{} voxels annotated(25%). Fitting-only class "
             "weights background/foreground {:.6f}/{:.6f}. First two actual volumes,each "
             "axial/coronal/sagittal,input|dense truth. Display clips[-1.2,1.2];truth dark "
             "background/green foreground.\n",
             annotated, 24 * 4096, weights.to_vector<float>()[0],
             weights.to_vector<float>()[1]);
}
```
