> Conclusion

Independent3D convolution,crop,normalization and loss derivatives precede initialized full-width checks and complete compact fitting. Sparse supervision,fit-only weights,current-volume inference BN and paired restoration remain explicit. Orthogonal slices and dense held-out metrics describe synthetic teaching volumes without medical or anatomical claims.

> References

- [Çiçek et al.(2016),3D U-Net: Learning Dense Volumetric Segmentation from Sparse Annotation](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.06650).
- [Milletari,Navab and Ahmadi(2016),V-Net: Fully Convolutional Neural Networks for Volumetric Medical Image Segmentation](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.04797).
